              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for weak, then the Marathi for to feel sick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पडसे",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पडसे — paḍse — \"a runny cold\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हवा बदलली की बाळाला पडसं होतं. havā badallī kī bāḷālā paḍsaṁ hotaṁ. When the weather changes the baby gets a runny cold."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पडसं होणे, with the dative. Sentences write the neuter as पडसं. Close to सर्दी."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पडसे (paḍse) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit pratiśyāya, \"a cold in the head\"; CDIAL lists Marathi paḍsẽ (CDIAL 8604)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
